-primordial-aa/1402882-whiskey-gin-and-teeth-arcane-wrote-some-things?p=1499582#post1499582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bad I genuinely forgot</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I actually didn't know if you had seen those or not, and wouldn't assume you had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-13-2022, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T19:36:13-08:00","id":1500080,"title":"","content":"Realization you probably already had. Don Quixote is a perfect example of a Hero. Not only does the themes of the book (especially the conflict of differing moral values respective of their times being great parallels to Beasts and Heroes struggling to find a place in the world) but also that the book itself ended up being taken by romantic writers as a tragic example of a lost ideal, despite the book being a scathing criticism of chivalry (the Hero wins and is beloved, no matter how ridiculous)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T21:47:39-08:00","id":1500256,"title":"","content":"I want this somewhere, so:<br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Introduction: &quot;Change is frightening but where there's fear, there's power. If We learn to feel our fear without letting it stop us, fear can become an ally, a sign to tell us that something we encountered can be transformed. Often our true strength is not in the things that represent what is familiar, comfortable, or positive but in our fear and even in our resistance to change&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-Starhawk, Dreaming the Dark</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 1: &quot;This is something I would find among doper friends, that, like, they will rob you and each other, but they also - there's an extent of protection, there's a clannishness that can feel real safe in an unsafe time. You can go, 'Well, Dave will rob me if I fall asleep, but he will protect me in case we run into trouble.'&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-John Darnielle, I Only Listen To The Mountain Goats, Episode 3: &quot;Color in Your Cheeks&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 2: &quot;young one, the things in this forest have claws and fangs</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">yes, we mean claws like the ones on your hands</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">yes, we mean fangs like the ones in your mouth</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">yes, we mean you should avoid things with claws and fangs</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">they are dangerous and only want to hurt you&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-On Being Raised on Fairy Tales in which You are the Monster</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 3: &quot;I ask of thee! Art thou Mankind?&quot;&quot;Nay! I am the world-the world inside the gourd.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-Gakuto Mikumo, The Mystic Archives of Dantalion</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 4: &quot;What would an ocean be without a monster lurking in the dark? It would be like a sleep without dreams.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-Werner Herzog</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 5: &quot;It takes a strong man to deny what's in front of him. And if the truth is undeniable, you create your own. The truth, Walker, is that you're here because you wanted to feel like something you're not: A hero.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-Col. John Konrad, Spec Ops: The Line</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 6: &quot;Holy places are dark places. It is life and strength, not knowledge and words, that we get in them. Holy wisdom is not clear and thin like water, but thick and dark like blood.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">-C.S. Lewis, 'Till We Have Faces</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chapter 7: \u201cIf you find yourself at a dead end and there\u2019s no other options left, doing something the wrong way might do the most good.\u201d</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u2013Junko Kaname, Puella Magi Madoka Magica</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-22-2022, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T05:03:57-08:00","id":1500366,"title":"","content":"Question about the introduction quote. Is the last word in the quote supposed to be &quot;chance&quot; or &quot;change?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpat